1 LABELS

   A label names a command line of a command procedure, for GOTO, GOSUB,
   and CALL.  It is a name of letters, digits, "$", and "_", starting
   with a letter, "$", or "_", followed by a colon at the start of the
   line, alone or before a command:

       $ LOOP:
       $ RETRY: COUNT = COUNT + 1

   A label belongs to its command level, and a label inside an IF block
   or a subroutine is reached only from within it.  At the terminal a
   label is ignored (DCL-W-NOLBLS).  See GOTO.
